\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid8143117\charrsid8143117 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 AudioPlayerAsset\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
 serves as an audio proxy that lets you easily change what sounds should be played. Having sound definitions spread out across separate asset files makes collaborating much easier, and managing them is done through the well-known Unity Project window inte
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 rface. Your programmers can link the asset in the right prefab, while your sound designer can tweak the asset itself without knowing exactly where it's played from.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The asset offers you a list of \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Conductors\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
. Each conductor has a filter that checks whether it should be played, and only the first allowed one is used. Conductors decide what to play and how, once the player is triggered. The framework comes with conductors that cover most use cases, but if you 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 need custom behaviour you can always extend them and make your own conductor type. Check the sample scene showcasing all conductor types. Here are the most notable conductor types:
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid8143117\charrsid8143117 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls6\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid8143117 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid8143117\charrsid8143117 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 PlayCollectionAudioConductor
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  - plays a sound picked from a list. Can play them in sequential, shuffle, or random order.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid8143117\charrsid8143117 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 PlayPitchSequenceConductor\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
 - plays the same sound every time, but changes the pitch according to your settings.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid8143117\charrsid8143117 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 IntroThenLoopConductor\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
 - plays an intro sound then loops another. Useful for music.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid8143117\charrsid8143117 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 LoopSequenceOverlappingConductor\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
 - loops sounds from a list by overlapping them (starts playing the next one before the last one finishes).
